1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,592
Where is the patient?

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:07,244
A patient is admitted, and planned for the ward.

3
00:00:07,594 --> 00:00:08,842
Admitted? Yes.

4
00:00:09,192 --> 00:00:11,336
Still in the Emergency Department? Maybe.

5
00:00:11,686 --> 00:00:13,510
Already in the ward? Maybe.

6
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:15,556
That uncertainty is the problem.

7
00:00:16,756 --> 00:00:18,420
The problem isn't the admission.

8
00:00:18,770 --> 00:00:21,458
It's knowing where the admitted patient actually is.

9
00:00:22,756 --> 00:00:25,396
Inpatient Pharmacy needs to know one simple thing:

10
00:00:25,746 --> 00:00:28,978
is the patient still in ED, or already in the ward?

11
00:00:32,928 --> 00:00:35,247
Every time the answer isn't immediately

12
00:00:35,247 --> 00:00:36,912
visible, someone has to ask.

13
00:00:38,112 --> 00:00:40,448
And Pharmacy's work depends on that answer.

14
00:00:44,312 --> 00:00:45,892
So what if the system itself could

15
00:00:45,892 --> 00:00:47,240
make that transition clearer?

16
00:00:47,590 --> 00:00:49,222
Here is an initial proposal.

17
00:00:49,572 --> 00:00:52,655
While the patient is still in ED, register them in

18
00:00:52,655 --> 00:00:55,060
PHIS at Kecemasan & Trauma (Admission).

19
00:00:56,260 --> 00:00:59,716
That location would mean: still at the ED admission stage.

20
00:01:00,066 --> 00:01:02,494
When the patient physically enters the ward, the

21
00:01:02,494 --> 00:01:04,770
location would be updated to the actual ward.

22
00:01:05,970 --> 00:01:08,556
But this is only an initial proposal. It must be

23
00:01:08,556 --> 00:01:10,658
validated, clinically and technically —

24
00:01:11,008 --> 00:01:14,176
including whether this is the correct PHIS mechanism.

25
00:01:15,376 --> 00:01:17,650
Under this initial proposal, the location

26
00:01:17,650 --> 00:01:19,424
would be updated in eight steps.

27
00:01:19,774 --> 00:01:21,405
In Visit Management, select

28
00:01:21,405 --> 00:01:24,606
Kecemasan & Trauma (Admission), and find the patient.

29
00:01:24,956 --> 00:01:27,276
Open the patient's visit, and click Edit.

30
00:01:27,626 --> 00:01:30,057
In the Transfer Detail List, select the

31
00:01:30,057 --> 00:01:31,802
new ward location, and save.

32
00:01:32,152 --> 00:01:33,854
The location would then move from

33
00:01:33,854 --> 00:01:35,144
ED admission to the ward.
